# Specification

30 entities.

## behavior `complete_task` — Complete a Task

`behaviors/task.spec:28`

**contract**

> When a CompleteTaskCommand is received for an existing task, the system MUST
> set the task status to `done`, set completedAt to the current time, and emit
> a task_completed event. An unknown task id MUST return TaskNotFoundError.
> It MUST return Result\<Task, TaskNotFoundError>.

**Fields**

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| category | command |

**Links**

| Field | Entity | Kind | Title |
|---|---|---|---|
| invariants | `completed_implies_timestamp` | invariant | Completed Tasks Have a Timestamp |
| types | `Task` | type | A unit of work the user wants to track |
| types | `CompleteTaskCommand` | type | — |
| types | `TaskNotFoundError` | type | — |
| ports | `TaskRepository` | port | Persistence boundary for tasks |
| produces | `task_completed` | event | Task Completed |
| features | `task_management` | feature | Task Management |
| satisfies | `no_lost_completion` | property | Completion is never lost |

**Verify**

| # | Kind | Obligation |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | unit | completing an unknown task returns TaskNotFoundError |
| 2 | unit | completing a task sets status to done |
| 3 | integration | task_completed event fires once per completion |

## behavior `create_task` — Create a Task

`behaviors/task.spec:10`

**contract**

> When a CreateTaskCommand is received, the system MUST reject an empty or
> whitespace-only title with InvalidTitleError, otherwise it MUST persist a
> new Task with status `open` and a unique id, then emit a task_created event.
> It MUST return Result\<Task, InvalidTitleError>.

**Fields**

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| category | command |

**Links**

| Field | Entity | Kind | Title |
|---|---|---|---|
| invariants | `task_id_uniqueness` | invariant | Task ID Uniqueness |
| types | `Task` | type | A unit of work the user wants to track |
| types | `CreateTaskCommand` | type | — |
| types | `InvalidTitleError` | type | — |
| ports | `TaskRepository` | port | Persistence boundary for tasks |
| produces | `task_created` | event | Task Created |
| features | `task_management` | feature | Task Management |

**Referenced by**

| Field | Entity | Kind | Title |
|---|---|---|---|
| constrains | `create_latency` | constraint | Task creation is fast |

**Verify**

| # | Kind | Obligation |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | unit | empty title is rejected |
| 2 | unit | valid title creates an open task |
| 3 | integration | created task is retrievable by id |

## behavior `list_tasks` — List Tasks by Status

`behaviors/task.spec:47`

**contract**

> When given a TaskStatus filter, the system MUST return all tasks with that
> status ordered by createdAt ascending. Listing cannot fail.

