## failure_mode `lost_task` — Task acknowledged but not persisted

`governance/decisions.spec:30`

**mitigation**

> Write within a SQLite transaction; flush before acknowledging

**Fields**

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| severity | high |
| occurrence | rare |
| detection | moderate |
| cause | Process killed between in-memory insert and disk flush |
| effect | User believes a task was saved but it disappears on restart |

**Links**

| Field | Entity | Kind | Title |
|---|---|---|---|
| invariant | `task_id_uniqueness` | invariant | Task ID Uniqueness |

## feature `task_management` — Task Management

`features/task_management.spec:3`

**problem**

> Users need to capture, track, and complete their work items.

**solution**

> Create, complete, and list tasks backed by a durable repository.

**Fields**

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| status | in_progress |
| priority | high |
| effort | m |

**acceptance**

- A user can create a task with a title
- A user can mark a task done
- A user can list tasks filtered by status

